      "provenance": {
        "molecular_model_reference": "SCM ADF 2026.1 official 3D-RISM documentation Table 7: a four-site united-atom ethanol model (H/O/CH2/CH3), independently re-expressed in Amber MDL units. Source density is 0.78546 g/cm3 at 298.15 K from Calvar et al.; nearby literature values vary slightly. The reported 17.0499 M input is the rounded conversion using the conventional ethanol molar mass 46.06844 g/mol. The explicit MDL site masses sum to 46.068 and define the site model, but are not the mass used for that 17.0499 M rounding. They follow the AmberTools 26 dat/leap/parm/parm10.dat convention C=12.01, H=1.008, O=16.00 amu, giving CH2=14.026 and CH3=15.034; source sha256 dc0c02d28fb7ee4f04d0a5edee3cd62968ba5e9bdb69e0f728bf01d242d7d062. ADF documentation also reports Weight=47.07; this file does not use that value. Sources: 3D-RISM Table 7 https://www.scm.com/doc/ADF/Input/3D-RISM.html; Calvar et al. https://doi.org/10.1021/je900998f; dielectric ThermoML https://trc.nist.gov/ThermoML/10.1021/je060248p.html",
